          "date": "2026-10-15 22:38:00.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity 160n",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity 160n\n\ntest_160n accumulates more than 65000 changelog records\nbefore racing changelog_clear against deletion. It did so\nwith createmany, a shell loop forking mrename 10001 times,\nand unlinkmany: 3 records per file, 30000 per pass, and\nthree passes (about 90000 records) to cross the target.\nThe mrename forks made it slow, 757s and 1057s on a VM.\n\nCreate and unlink files instead, 2 records per file (CREAT\nand UNLNK), until 66000 records are reached: a single pass\nof 33000 files normally. The fail_loc race section is\nunchanged. On a VM the test now takes 43s and 27s.\n\nCap the per-pass count to MDT0's free inodes less a margin,\nso a small MDT takes extra passes instead of failing with\nENOSPC, and size the last pass to what is still needed.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=160n\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I0ee83e7e21f8ab0423d3c7fc8a6ba0742af5872e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
